From: mova
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/tls_mbedtls: keep the DTLS-SRTP profile list alive

mbedtls_ssl_conf_dtls_srtp_protection_profiles() stores the pointer, not a copy. The list was a
stack array in tls_open(), so the handshake later read a dangling pointer. On Android arm64
(mbedtls 3.4.0) the stale stack had been overwritten, the ServerHello carried no use_srtp
extension and the peer answered insufficient_security (alert 71). Make the array static const.

diff --git a/libavformat/tls_mbedtls.c b/libavformat/tls_mbedtls.c
--- a/libavformat/tls_mbedtls.c
+++ b/libavformat/tls_mbedtls.c
@@ -560,7 +560,8 @@
     uint32_t verify_res_flags;
     int ret;
 #if defined(MBEDTLS_SSL_DTLS_SRTP)
-    const mbedtls_ssl_srtp_profile profiles[] = {
+    /* mbedtls_ssl_conf_dtls_srtp_protection_profiles() keeps the pointer, so the list must outlive tls_open() */
+    static const mbedtls_ssl_srtp_profile profiles[] = {
         MBEDTLS_TLS_SRTP_AES128_CM_HMAC_SHA1_80,
         MBEDTLS_TLS_SRTP_UNSET
     };
